# {{.Name}}

An ultrastack product: business logic only, everything else is the paved
road. The framework's full skill lives in the ultrastack repo's SKILL.md;
this file covers what is product-specific.

## The rules of this repo

- `main.go` never grows. `Modules()` in `modules.go` is the whole assembly;
  business logic lives in modules like `HelloModule` — providers +
  `stack.Route`s + `di.Export`s.
- Every route declares its policy: `Require: "{{.Name}}.read"` (permission),
  `Require: "policy:name"` (custom Policy), or `Public: true`. The zero
  value means "any authenticated caller" — safe by default.
- Config = `config.toml` sections bound to typed structs
  (`conf.Section[T]("name")`); `[auth.roles]` hot-reloads. Env overrides:
  `ULTRA_<SECTION>_<FIELD>`. Print the always-current reference:
  `go run . config reference`.
- After ANY wiring change, run the covenant: `go test -run TestWiring ./...`
  — the error text names the fix; `ultra explain DIxxxx` teaches the code.

## Commands (the binary is a toolbox)

```
go run .                    # serve
go run . routes             # auth-requirement table
go run . graph | blast      # graph summary / blast radius
go run . config reference   # annotated config docs
```

Add a command by providing `cli.Command` from any module (Boot: true for
commands needing live components — they start ONLY their own deps).

## Testing layers

1. unit: hand-construct (di.Many literals, di.Some/None, di.LazyOf,
   di.ScopeFunc, di.FamilyFixed, di.SyncRunner) — never the container
2. wiring: `TestWiring` (stack.Validate)
3. integration: `di.TestApp(t, di.Options(Modules()...), di.Swap[X](fake))`
